---
args: { ledger: FacilityVisitLedger, caseId: ID, receipt: FacilityVisitReceipt, plannedLocationId: ID, plannedIssueIds: ID[], requiredCheckIds: ID[], authorizedVisit: VisitAccessPermission | null, consentStatusAtAttempt: "valid" | "expired" | "unknown" }
returns: FacilityVisitReconciliation
---
1. If receipt.receiptId is consumed, compare every field to the stored receipt. On exact replay bind assessment = interpretVisitEvidence(caseId, stored receipt, plannedLocationId, plannedIssueIds, requiredCheckIds, authorizedVisit, consentStatusAtAttempt); bind result = { ledger, outcome: "replayed", resolution: assessment.resolution, nextActions: assessment.nextActions }; return unchanged. For a conflicting or unbound ID bind result = { ledger, outcome: "held", resolution: "unknown", nextActions: ["reconcile receipt identity and visit record"] }; return unchanged.
2. Bind assessment = interpretVisitEvidence(caseId, receipt, plannedLocationId, plannedIssueIds, requiredCheckIds, authorizedVisit, consentStatusAtAttempt). Let its binding and resolution consume the exact work, access, verification, and residual-symptom findings.
3. Append every newly observed receipt exactly once, including held, partial, and unknown outcomes; add its ID once to consumedReceiptIds and increment the ledger revision once. Preserve all earlier attempts.
4. Bind nextActions to assessment.nextActions plus assessment.missingCheckIds and assessment.reasons. Bind outcome = "recorded" when assessment.binding is "valid", otherwise "held". Bind result = { ledger: updatedLedger, outcome, resolution: assessment.resolution, nextActions }; return result. A duplicate receipt never adds another visit; a fresh consented window is required after failed access; recurring work remains open until the technical and occupant or objective evidence supports closure.
